  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2021-11-04T13:07:00.354Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Avatar ripping is a big problem for avatar creators and if we want to keep growing the vrc community we need to make sure that these creators dont get discouraged from making good content. Therefore creating a system that can prevent this is very important for the longevity of the platform. \nMy understanding of NFTs is that its a decentralized way of keeping track of ownership of digital assets. My idea is to implement an avatar NFT check in vrc so when an avatar ccreator sells a model the NFT is sold along with the model. This model is uploaded along side with the NFT to vrc and when a player loads an avatar its NFT is checked against the blockchain registry. If the NFT on the model doesnt match the most recent owner the player would not be allowed to use that avatar.\nDisclaimer: My understanding of NFTs is quite basic so this might not be technically feasible.",
